before:
Complete local Java example; the app itself does not execute it:
```java
import java.time.*;
public class Main {

  public static void main(String[] args) {
    Instant point = Instant.parse("2025-01-01T00:30:00Z");
    System.out.println(point.atZone(ZoneId.of("UTC")).toLocalDate());
    System.out.println(point.atZone(ZoneId.of("America/New_York")).toLocalDate());
  }
}
```

after:
Read the same instant in UTC and New York. In this January example, New York is five hours behind UTC.

```java
import java.time.*;
public class Main {

  public static void main(String[] args) {
    Instant point = Instant.parse("2025-01-01T00:30:00Z");
    System.out.println(point.atZone(ZoneId.of("UTC")).toLocalDate());
    System.out.println(point.atZone(ZoneId.of("America/New_York")).toLocalDate());
  }
}
```
